<div id="privacy-modal" class="privacy-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="privacy-modal-title" hidden>
  <div class="privacy-modal__backdrop" id="privacy-modal-backdrop"></div>
  <div class="privacy-modal__panel">
    <div class="privacy-modal__header">
      <h2 id="privacy-modal-title">Privacy Notice</h2>
      <button type="button" id="privacy-modal-close" class="privacy-modal__close" aria-label="Close privacy notice">&times;</button>
    </div>
    <div class="privacy-modal__body">
      <p>This site is run by <strong><%= siteName %></strong>, who is responsible for the data described here.
        <% if (privacyEmail) { %>Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:<%= privacyEmail %>"><%= privacyEmail %></a>.<% } else { %>For questions or requests, contact the site owner using the contact details on this site.<% } %></p>

      <h3>What's collected</h3>
      <p>When you view a page, the site records the page, the time, the page that linked you here, your browser's user-agent string, and the country you're visiting from (as reported by Cloudflare). Your IP address is not stored. Only a one-way, keyed hash of it is kept to tell repeat visits apart.</p>

      <h3>Why</h3>
      <p>To understand how the site is used. The legal basis is the owner's legitimate interest in running and improving the site (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).</p>

      <h3>Cookies</h3>
      <p>Visitors get no cookies. Your browser's local storage remembers that you dismissed the notice banner, and nothing else. A session cookie is only set when the site owner logs into the admin area.</p>

      <h3>How long</h3>
      <p>Visit records are deleted automatically after 90 days.</p>

      <h3>Who else sees it</h3>
      <p>Data is never sold or shared. The site runs on a DigitalOcean server and is delivered through Cloudflare. Both process requests on the owner's behalf only to serve the site, and may do so outside your country under their standard data-protection terms.</p>

      <h3>Your rights</h3>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you can ask to access, correct or delete your data, or object to its collection<% if (privacyEmail) { %> by emailing <a href="mailto:<%= privacyEmail %>"><%= privacyEmail %></a><% } else { %> by contacting the site owner<% } %>. You can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

      <p class="privacy-modal__meta">Last updated September 30, 2026 · Built on <a href="https://github.com/lucas-iezzi/open-folio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open-folio</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
